WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.690
Scarlet Witch has a long history in the comics,
and with Wandavision, she's finally getting

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:08.970
her turn on the center stage of the Marvel
Cinematic Universe.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:13.559
But even when she was more of a background
player, the MCU has been dropping Easter eggs

00:00:13.559 --> 00:00:15.940
about her long history in Marvel comics.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.930
It can sometimes take a while for Marvel Cinematic
Universe characters to take on the colorful

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:22.960
names of their comic book counterparts.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:28.679
For example, Rhodey was only offhandedly referred
to as a "war machine" by Tony Stark in Iron

00:00:28.679 --> 00:00:34.440
Man 2, and he didn't officially assume that
moniker until Iron Man 3.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:39.769
Wanda Maximoff, on the other hand, has never
been called Scarlet Witch in any MCU film

00:00:39.769 --> 00:00:44.200
— although she did finally acquire the name
in an episode of WandaVision.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.579
"This is chaos magic, Wanda.

00:00:47.579 --> 00:00:53.399
That makes you the Scarlet Witch."

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:58.611
Prior to that Disney+ program, the closest
audiences had gotten to seeing Wanda Maximoff

00:00:58.611 --> 00:01:04.000
being called Scarlet Witch came during a small
piece of dialogue in Avengers: Age of Ultron.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.990
In a scene when Tony Stark tries to calm Hulk
down after he's been enraged by Wanda Maximoff's

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:14.770
superpowers, Stark makes an early nod to Wanda's
comics name.

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:17.720
"That little witch is messing with your mind.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:18.750
You're stronger than her.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:20.280
You're smarter than her.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.610
You're Bruce Banner."

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:27.340
Wanda never referred to herself as any kind
of witch during her subsequent film appearances,

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:33.040
but it seems likely that after WandaVision,
she'll own her superhero alter ego — Marvel

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:37.909
Studios chief Kevin Feige promised audiences
that WandaVision would see the character finally

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:39.670
become Scarlet Witch.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:45.200
Wanda was introduced to the Marvel Cinematic
Universe before Disney purchased Fox, which

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:49.510
meant significant portions of her comics backstory
needed to be changed.

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:55.060
Because Wanda in the comics was both supposedly
a mutant and a mainstay on the Avengers team,

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:58.390
both companies had the rights to use the character
on screen.

00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:03.131
However, both studios were restricted on what
they could do with Wanda — as well as her

00:02:03.131 --> 00:02:06.390
brother Pietro Maximoff, a.k.a. Quicksilver.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:11.590
For Marvel Studios, this shared custody agreement
meant that they could use Wanda, but couldn't

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:15.310
make her a mutant — or, obviously, the daughter
of Magneto.

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:20.320
Thus, while Wanda still has a twin brother
named Pietro Maximoff in the MCU, her parents

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:21.830
are normal human beings.

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:26.370
Another part of her origin story that was
altered: The MCU's version of Wanda hails

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:31.420
from the European country of Sokovia rather
than her original comic book country of origin,

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:32.420
Transia.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:37.280
Though the names of the countries have changed,
Sokovia bears more than a passing resemblance

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.000
to Wanda's original homeland.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:44.620
Like Transia, Sokovia is a fictional Eastern
European country rife with political turmoil

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:48.910
— making it a subtle nod to Wanda Maximoff's
original home for comics fans.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:53.610
Not all superheroes start out as superheroes.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:57.920
Some start out like Tony Stark — arrogant
people so blinded by their own wealth that

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.630
they can't see how their actions affect others.

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:05.990
Other superheroes begin their journeys as
outright supervillains — like Wanda Maximoff.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:10.480
She and her brother Pietro began their time
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe as voluntary

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:14.030
human guinea pigs for the terrorist organization
known as Hydra.

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:19.210
These experiments gave them both their superpowers,
and they eventually joined forces with the

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:23.100
diabolical robot Ultron as his super-powered
henchmen.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:28.020
In their time working for Ultron, Wanda and
her brother tormented the Avengers and helped

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:31.840
lay the groundwork for the maniacal robot's
plan for world domination.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:37.850
While this is different from the duo's origin
story in the comics, it isn't a complete change

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:41.000
— Wanda also started out as a villain there
as well.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:45.550
There, she and Pietro, as the children of
Magneto, were critical figures in the Brotherhood

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:48.400
of Mutants and frequently fought the X-Men.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:53.050
Much like their film incarnations, though,
Wanda and Pietro didn't stay villainous for

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:54.210
long.

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:55.879
"How could you?

00:03:55.879 --> 00:03:56.879
"

00:03:56.879 --> 00:03:57.900
"How could I what?"

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:02.540
"You said we would destroy the Avengers make
a better world."

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:03.540
"It will be better."

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:09.320
In both mediums, they eventually turned against
their evil masters and went on to work for

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:13.480
the Avengers — just as comics readers always
suspected they would.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:18.150
The suburban New Jersey setting of WandaVision
is a gift that keeps on giving.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:23.100
On the surface, it allows the show to pay
homage to classic sitcoms, many of which also

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.790
take place in the suburbs.

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:29.980
It works for the show, but it wasn't just
invented for TV — this superhero duo's New

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:34.811
Jersey roots actually go all the way back
to an offbeat storyline in the 1985 comic

00:04:34.811 --> 00:04:36.790
series The Vision and the Scarlet Witch.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:41.430
In that series, the couple moves to the New
Jersey suburbs after getting married to enjoy

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:42.890
a life together.

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:47.210
Unfortunately, it isn't that easy — the
locals aren't happy with a human/android marriage

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:48.690
happening in their community.

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:53.930
That source of conflict in The Vision and
Scarlet Witch is more mundane than the supernatural

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:58.790
goings-on that fuel the plot of WandaVision,
but putting the pair in Westview adds connective

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:04.980
tissue to Wanda and Vision's prior comic book
series — as well as 2016's Vision series,

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:09.500
which saw the character of Vision once again
retreating to the suburbs with a new synthezoid

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:10.500
family.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:16.150
In the MCU, Hawkeye and Wanda Maximoff have
developed a close bond since meeting in Avengers:

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:17.220
Age of Ultron.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:22.160
Their first big meeting didn't seem to signal
that dynamic, though, as it entailed Wanda,

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:26.970
still working as a minion of Ultron, trying
to sneak up on Hawkeye only for the archer

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:30.070
to plug an electric arrow onto her forehead.

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:35.560
However, the two superheroes grew closer once
Wanda defected to the Avengers.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:40.920
This was solidified by the climax of Age of
Ultron, which saw Hawkeye giving Wanda a big

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:43.700
speech about what it means to be an Avenger.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:50.630
"The city is flying, we're fighting an army
of robots, and I have a bow and arrow.

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:53.830
None of this makes sense."

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:58.000
His rapport with Wanda took on a paternal
sense of protection after her brother Pietro

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.550
sacrificed himself to save Hawkeye.

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:06.270
Just like that, she had lost the only family
she had left in the world -- so Hawkeye stepped

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:09.460
in to help her feel like she still had somewhere
she belonged.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:13.980
The pair has also had a close bond in the
comics, though it's been more complicated

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:14.980
there.

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:19.780
Instead of having paternal feelings for Wanda,
in the comics Hawkeye sees her more as a romantic

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:23.760
interest -- at least, until Vision shows up
in her life.

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:27.520
While their relationship has been altered
for the movies, Hawkeye and Wanda's closeness

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:30.520
in the MCU echoes the comics that came before
it.

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:35.420
Though WandaVision marks the first time Wanda
Maximoff has used her superpowers to create

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:40.389
a persistent alternate reality in the Marvel
Cinematic Universe, it's something she's accomplished

00:06:40.389 --> 00:06:43.090
in the comics before -- more than once.

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:47.139
Her abilities in this department were most
famously the crux of the comic book storyline

00:06:47.139 --> 00:06:51.200
House of M, which was penned by Brian Michael
Bendis in 2005.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:56.760
Here Wanda, much like in WandaVision, is in
a period of deep emotional distress — though

00:06:56.760 --> 00:07:02.210
in House of M her grief is the result of losing
her children, not losing Vision.

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:08.710
To cope with her crushing sadness, Wanda decides
to escape by creating her own alternate reality.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:13.210
This decision doesn't just impact Wanda, though
— it sends the entire Marvel Universe into

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:18.250
chaos, creating a world run by mutants, under
the cold rule of the family of Magneto.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:22.341
When the rest of the heroes in the Marvel
universe wake up to what's going on, they're

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:27.870
forced to come together to stop Wanda at any
cost and set the world right again.

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:33.060
Looking at House of M's broad strokes, it's
clear WandaVision takes cues from this comics

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:40.490
event, including the emphasis on Wanda navigating
very real emotional problems through her superpowers.

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:44.930
There are clear and major differences between
the comics and the show, but the similarities

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:48.210
between the two are impossible to miss.

